rem Diophantine Reciprocals II
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=110
rem Find the least n for which 1/x + 1/y
rem = 1/n has more than a target number
rem of solutions

use sequences
use io
use cli

option Target integer = 4000000

rem Solutions number (d(n^2) + 1) / 2,
rem and d(n^2) is the product of 2e + 1
rem over the prime exponents e of n. The
rem least n takes the smallest primes
rem with exponents never increasing.
rem Grow the candidates one prime at a
rem time.
Need = Target * 2 - 1
Ps = primes take 16 array
Best = Ps reduce *
Exp = 1 to 60 array
Cols = Exp reshape 1 60
N = array 1
Cnt = array 1
Top = array 60
for P in Ps
  Rows = N len
  Big = N (P ** Exp) outer *
  Level' = (N * 0) Exp outer +
  Cap' = Top reshape Rows 1 at least Cols
  Fit = Cap and Big less Best
  Next = Cnt (Exp * 2 + 1) outer *
  Done' = Fit and Next greater Need
  Hits' = Big filter Done
  Pool' = concat (array Best) Hits
  Best = Pool min
  Keep = Fit and Next at most Need
  Top = Level filter Keep array
  N = Big filter Keep array
  Cnt = Next filter Keep array
end
Answer = Best
Answer print
